        "original_id": "28aaf0cf-4fad-5c83-a3bd-0ee1c8e76265",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jayaprakash Narayan\n- Organizations: People's Union for Civil Liberties\n- Awards: Bharat Ratna\n- Places: India\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Jayaprakash Narayan formed the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights in India.\n- The People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights later became the People's Union for Civil Liberties.\n- The People's Union for Civil Liberties is a human rights body in India.\n- The Bharat Ratna is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\n- In 1999, Jayaprakash Narayan was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna in recognition of his social work.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7030d0b1-bc70-5c0c-91b8-36835e9bbdb1",
        "text": "Page: Jayaprakash Narayan. Sentence: In 1999, he was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna, India's highest civilian award, in recognition of his social work.\nPage: Bharat Ratna. Sentence: The Bharat Ratna (] ; \"Jewel of India\") is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\nPage: People's Union for Civil Liberties. Sentence: People's Union for Civil Liberties (PUCL) is a human rights body formed in India in 1976 by socialist leader Jayaprakash Narayan, as the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights (PUCLDR).",
